Injection points for the port's tests, at five of Apache Cloudberry's
faults inside PostgreSQL's own replication code, which its FTS tests in
isolation2 hold or count (src/test/isolation2/sql/segwalrep):

  wal-sender-loop        walsender.c, WalSndLoop()        wal_sender_loop
  wal-sender-after-send  walsender.c, WalSndLoop()        wal_sender_after_caughtup_within_range
  walrecv-skip-flush     walreceiver.c, XLogWalRcvFlush() walrecv_skip_flush
  sync-rep-query-die     syncrep.c, SyncRepWaitForLSN()   sync_rep_query_die
  sync-rep-query-cancel  syncrep.c, SyncRepWaitForLSN()   sync_rep_query_cancel

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c); walrecv-skip-flush is given a bool its callback sets to skip
the flush.  They serve tests alone, so they are not in the core series:
Dockerfile.pg applies this to the tree of either ref, vanilla or patched,
so that the two images still differ only in the ref.  Dormant, as any
point is: without injection points the macro is empty, and with them a
point nothing attached to runs no callback.


